# What never belongs in a build context.
#
# Two reasons, and the second is the one that cost a build. Every image here is
# built from the repository root, so without this the daemon receives 2.9GB of
# which 2.2GB is provisioned output nothing in an image uses.
#
# The one that bites: `web.Dockerfile` installs the console's dependencies from
# its lockfile and then copies the console in. With `console/node_modules`
# present in the context, that copy lands a developer machine's tree on top of
# the one just installed, pnpm finds a modules directory that does not match
# the lockfile, and the build fails asking for a TTY to confirm removing it.
# Nothing in that message mentions a build context.

.git
.github

# Provisioned, not authored. Reinstalled inside the image from the lockfiles.
.venv
console/node_modules
console/.toolchain

# Build output. Every image builds its own; a stale one copied in is a
# deployment serving something nobody built here.
console/.next
docs/site/build
build
dist

# Test and tool residue.
console/test-results
console/playwright-report
**/__pycache__
.pytest_cache
.mypy_cache
.ruff_cache
.coverage
htmlcov

# Not part of any image, and large.
_research
.codegraph
specs
